// The **package orphan rule** (E0070): an `impl Trait for Type` must live in the same package as
// the trait or as the type. Here a third package — `glue`, a transitive dependency this entry does
// not name once — implements `a`'s trait for `b`'s type.
//
// That is exactly the injection the rule exists to stop. Without it this program ran: `Thing`
// silently satisfied `Speaks`, `t.speak()` dispatched into code from a package the author never
// wrote down, and a second such package anywhere in the graph collided as an E0027 the end user
// could not fix — they own neither impl, so they can remove neither.
//
// A **package** case: subdirectories of the case directory are dependency packages, which is the
// only form that can express a package boundary at all (a flat directory is one package).
// expect: error E0070 at 8:6
// expect: exit 1
use b.thing.{Thing};

echo Thing.new(7).id
